CORE
main.c
--datarace --no-assertions --por --unwind 2 --rounds 7 --index-chain --allow-pointer-unsoundness
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^index chain: [1-9][0-9]* of
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Both accesses of x are under the mutex, so there is no race. Mutual exclusion
goes through the mutex's chain, which --index-chain may also turn into an index
chain: a wrong decode there would let both threads into the critical section
and report a race the program does not have.
